Proposed (11.1s): Use this skill any time work on the ttaccessible app involves user-facing text in the UI — adding or changing a button label, menu item, tooltip, alert or error message, dialog text, preferences label, placeholder, accessibility label, or VoiceOver announcement. ttaccessible is a bilingual macOS app (English + French), so ANY new visible string must be added to both en.lproj/Localizable.strings and fr.lproj/Localizable.strings with French in vouvoiement. Trigger on phrases like "add a button that says…", "show an alert when…", "the tooltip should read…", "label this menu item…", "the accessibility label should be…", or any French-language request to ajouter/traduire un texte. Also trigger on explicit mentions of Localizable.strings, L10n.text, L10n.format, fr.lproj, en.lproj, or translation work. If the user is creating a new piece of UI copy of any kind, this skill applies — do NOT wait for them to mention localization explicitly.

